{"schema_version":"1.7.3","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:20312-1","published":"2026-03-04T10:51:24Z","modified":"2026-03-05T21:15:10.380704Z","related":["CVE-2025-10911","CVE-2025-8732","CVE-2026-0990","CVE-2026-0992","CVE-2026-1757"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-10911","CVE-2025-8732","CVE-2026-0990","CVE-2026-0992","CVE-2026-1757"],"summary":"Security update for libxml2, libxslt","details":"This update for libxml2, libxslt fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in libxml2:\n\n- CVE-2026-0990: call stack overflow may lead to application crash due to infinite recursion in\n  `xmlCatalogXMLResolveURI` (bsc#1256807, bsc#1256811).\n- CVE-2026-0992: excessive resource consumption when processing XML catalogs due to exponential behavior when handling\n  `nextCatalog` elements (bsc#1256809, bsc#1256812).\n- CVE-2025-8732: infinite recursion in catalog parsing functions when processing malformed SGML catalog files\n  (bsc#1247858).\n- CVE-2026-1757: memory leak in the `xmllint` interactive shell (bsc#1257594, bsc#1257595).\n- CVE-2025-10911: parsing xsl nodes may lead to use-after-free with key data stored cross-RVT (bsc#1250553)\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libxml2","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/libxml2&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.13.8-160000.4.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libexslt0":"1.1.43-160000.4.1","libxml2-2":"2.13.8-160000.4.1","libxml2-devel":"2.13.8-160000.4.1","libxml2-doc":"2.13.8-160000.4.1","libxml2-tools":"2.13.8-160000.4.1","libxslt-devel":"1.1.43-160000.4.1","libxslt-tools":"1.1.43-160000.4.1","libxslt1":"1.1.43-160000.4.1","python313-libxml2":"2.13.8-160000.4.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/openSUSE-SU-2026:20312-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libxml2-python","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/libxml2-python&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events